== Problem description ==
Samsung Z Fold 4 displays the charging animation but never boots. Acts as if charging but battery percentage does not increase.

[[File:Z Fold 4 5G Fake Charging.jpg|thumb|Z Fold 4 5G - Fake Charging]]
[[File:ASL01 CHARGE.png|thumb|Z Fold 4 5G - ASL01 Charging IC]]

== Symptoms ==

* Shows charging symbol only
* Stays stuck on charging logo
* Battery percentage does not increase
* Phone does not power on normally
* V_BATT line measuring 0 Ω (dead short)

== Solution ==
The failure is caused by a short on the V_BATT power rail, usually due to a failed ASL01 power IC.

Removing the IC clears the short; replacing it resolves fake charging permanently.

[[File:VBATT.png|thumb|Z Fold 4 5G - VBATT Line Diode Mode Reading]]
[[File:ASL01 IC LOCATION BOARDVIEW.png|thumb|Z Fold 4 5G - ASL01 IC Location On BoardView]]

=== Diagnostic Steps ===

=== 1. Visual Inspection ===

* Check the mainboard for corrosion or burn marks.
* Inspect USB-C daughterboard, battery connector, and PMIC areas.
* Ensure no aftermarket battery is causing brownout behavior.

----

=== 2. Diode Mode – V_BATT Rail Check ===

* Probe the V_BATT test point / capacitor bank near the FPC connectors.
* Expected normal reading: typically in the hundreds of kΩ or >1MΩ.
* Faulty board reading : 0.09 Ω → confirmed short.

----

=== 3. Short Hunting ===

* Use multimeter continuity across the V_BATT line.
* Use thermal cam or voltage injection (1 V, limited to 1–2 A).
* In this case, no component heated visibly during first injection.
* Move to boardview/diagram → V_BATT rail maps to ASL01 Charging IC (Located right next to the Battery Connector FPC).

----

=== 4. Confirm Shorted IC ===

* Apply rosin + re-inject voltage.
* ASL01 IC heats up → confirmed bad component.

=== Repair Steps ===

=== 1. Remove the Faulty ASL01 IC ===

* Mask surrounding components with high temperature tape.
* Apply hot air.
* Gently lift the ASL01 IC.

=== 2. Re-Test the V_BATT Rail ===

* Measure at same point as initial short.
* After IC removal: reading becomes 19 MΩ.
* This confirms the short is fully cleared.

=== 3. Install New ASL01 IC ===

* Clean pads with solder wick + flux.
* Apply fresh leaded solder.
* Reball or use pre-balled IC.
* Align and solder the new ASL01 Charging IC.

=== 4. Final Measurement ===

* After reinstallation, check V_BATT again:
** Reading becomes 2.16 kΩ / .469V (normal range from reference).

=== 5. Assemble & Boot Test ===

* Reconnect battery and screen.
* Phone now boots normally and charges correctly.